I understand your frustration, and I'm sorry to hear that your game freezes when the collision happens. It’s common for newcomers to HTML5 projects to run into exactly that issue, usually because the event listener isn’t binding in the right context or because the object reference is altered subtly.

Here is the crash-free version of that collision section. Make sure your `player` object has properties `x`, `y`, `w` (width), and `h` (height).  `score` and `endGame` have been added for full functionality.

